# Bytes that are hashed or compared byte for byte keep LF on every checkout,
# so a Windows clone with core.autocrlf reads what Linux and macOS read.
#
# design/ holds the SDK's design files; every file kit generates from one
# names it with the sha256 of its bytes, and `tools/genindex -check-api
# -digests` hashes them again (tools/genindex/CLAUDE.md).
design/** text eol=lf
# The files kit generates, every one named gen_* (kit's ADR 0014): the pins,
# the ports, the codes, the facade, the declarations. Their headers carry the
# sha256 of their own body.
**/gen_*.go text eol=lf
# docs/api is written by `make api` and compared byte for byte by
# `make api-check`.
docs/api/** text eol=lf
# The platforms table genindex reads without running it.
scripts/ci/platforms.sh text eol=lf
# The json and ndjson goldens (#893) are the bytes encoding/json v1 wrote,
# compared byte for byte by the codecs' identity tests: a CRLF checkout would
# fail them on a codec that writes LF.
internal/service/data/codec/json/testdata/golden/** text eol=lf
internal/service/data/codec/ndjson/testdata/golden/** text eol=lf
pkg/v1/data/codec/testdata/json-golden/** text eol=lf
